        "evidence_id": "pdfplumber:abstract",
        "source": "pdf_layout",
        "field": "abstract",
        "raw_text": "We present new lattice-based attribute-based encryption (ABE) and laconic function evaluation (LFE) schemes for circuits with sublinear ciphertext overhead. For depth d circuits over (cid:2)-bit inputs, we obtain - an ABE with ciphertext and secret key size O(1); - a LFE with ciphertext size (cid:2)+O(1) and digest size O(1); - an ABE with public key and ciphertext size O((cid:2)2/3) and secret key size O(1), where O(·) hides poly(d,λ) factors. The first two results achieve almost optimal ciphertext and secret key/digest sizes, up to the poly(d) depen- dencies.Thesecurityofourschemesrelieson(cid:2)-succinctLWE,afalsifiable assumption which is implied by evasive LWE. At the core of our results is a new technique for compressing LWE samples s(A−x⊗G) as well as the matrix A.",
